      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that a signature starting with bytes `0x53, 0x2A, 0x00...` doesn't match Zstandard format — `0x53` looks like a skippable frame candidate (high nibble `0x5`), but the remaining bytes don't match `SKIPPABLE_FRAME_MAGIC`. I'll write a more readable version.Now I'll compile-check the test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces the opaque `test2` method name and `byteArray0`/`boolean0` variable names with descriptive identifiers and a comment explaining exactly why the skippable-frame path is entered but ultimately returns false."
